alid day is 22 (2+2=4). June 22nd:06/22. Sum:0+6+2+2=10.\n\nMay (05): 0+5=5. Day digits sum to 5. Max day: 32 (invalid). So 32 is invalid, so 23 (2+3=5). May 23rd:05/23. Sum:0+5+2+3=10.\n\nApril (04): 0+4=4. Day digits sum to 6. Max day: 33 (invalid). Next is 24 (2+4=6). April 24th:04/24. Sum:0+4+2+4=10.\n\nMarch (03): 0+3=3. Day digits sum to 7. Max day: 31 (3+1=4). Wait, sum to 7: 25 (2+5=7), 16 (1+6=7), 07 (0+7=7). Max day is 25. March 25th:03/25. Sum:0+3+2+5=10.\n\nFebruary (02): 0+2=2. Day digits sum to 8. Since 2008 is a leap year, February has 29 days. Max day where digits sum to 8: 26 (2+6=8), 17 (1+7=8), 08 (0+8=8). Max day is 26. February 26th:02/26. Sum:0+2+2+6=10.\n\nJanuary (01): 0+1=1. Day digits sum to 9. Max day: 31 (3+1=4). So days where digits sum to 9: 18 (1+8=9), 27 (2+7=9). Max day is 27. January 27th:01/27. Sum:0+1+2+7=10.\n\nSo, compiling all these dates:\n\n- January 27: 01/27\n- February 26:02/26\n- March 25:03/25\n- April 24:04/24\n- May 23:05/23\n- June 22:06/22\n- July 30:07/30\n- August 20:08/20\n- September 10:09/10\n- October 27:10/27\n- November 26:11/26\n- December 25:12/25\n\nSo, the latest date in this list is December 25th. Therefore, December 25, 2008 is the last occurrence in 2008 where the sum of the first four digits equals the sum of the last four digits.\n\nBut wait, just to ensure that there are no errors in this reasoning. Let's confirm the December 25th date again. The date is written as 12/25/2008. First four digits: 1, 2, 2, 5. Sum:1+2+2+5=10. Last four digits:2,0,0,8. Sum:2+0+0+8=10. Correct. And December 25th is a valid date. December does have 31 days, so 25 is valid.\n\nBut let's check if there's a later date in December with sum 10. Suppose there's a date like 12/3X where X is some digit. For example, 12/31: sum 1+2+3+1=7. 12/30: sum 6. 12/29:14. 12/28:13. 12/27:12. 12/26:11. 12/25:10. So after 25th, no dates with sum 10. So December 25th is indeed the latest.\n\nAlternatively, is there a date in December where the